{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":174592,"duration_api_ms":172534,"num_turns":25,"result":"Perfect! I have successfully produced the WDD (Workflow Definition Document) for the 1000genome workflow. Here is the complete file content:\n\n```yaml\nmetadata:\n  workflow_lineage_id: wrd:1000genome\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  version_notes: \"Initial WDD compiled from daxgen.py and bin/ tasks\"\n  deprecated: false\n  workflow_name: 1000-genome\n  workflow_description: \"The 1000 Genomes workflow analyzes human genetic variation by processing SNP (Single Nucleotide Polymorphism) variant data from the 1000 Genomes Project. It fetches and parses Phase3 VCF files by chromosome, extracts per-individual genotype information, cross-matches mutation data with SIFT scores (effect prediction), and performs statistical analysis to identify overlapping mutations across individuals by population. The workflow computes mutation frequency distributions and generates overlap statistics to provide a null distribution for rigorous statistical evaluation of potential disease-related mutations.\"\n  source_repository: \"/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow\"\n  source_commit: null\n  source_format: compiled_from_pegasus_dax\n  source_file: daxgen.py\n  schema_version: \"wrd-7.0\"\n  generated_by: claude-haiku-4-5\n  generated_at: \"2026-03-11T00:00:00Z\"\n  last_modified_at: \"2026-03-11T00:00:00Z\"\n\nstages:\n  - stage_id: stage:input_preparation\n    name: Input Preparation\n    order: 1\n    description: \"Load reference data files including VCF chromosome files, population metadata, and SIFT variant effect prediction annotations.\"\n    tasks: []\n\n  - stage_id: stage:individuals_processing\n    name: Individuals Processing\n    order: 2\n    description: \"Parse VCF files by chromosome into per-individual genotype records. Multiple parallel jobs process chunks of each chromosome file, then merge results.\"\n    tasks:\n      - task:individuals\n      - task:individuals_merge\n\n  - stage_id: stage:variant_effect_prediction\n    name: Variant Effect Prediction\n    order: 3\n    description: \"Filter and annotate variants with SIFT scores indicating predicted phenotypic effect of SNP substitutions.\"\n    tasks:\n      - task:sifting\n\n  - stage_id: stage:mutation_analysis\n    name: Mutation Analysis\n    order: 4\n    description: \"Analyze overlapping mutations across individuals stratified by population, and compute frequency distributions of overlaps.\"\n    tasks:\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n\ntasks:\n  - task_id: task:individuals\n    name: Individuals\n    stage: stage:individuals_processing\n    executable: bin/individuals.py\n    description: \"Parse a VCF file for a single chromosome, extracting genotype data for each individual. This task processes a contiguous range of rows from the input VCF file (one chunk per job) and creates per-individual output files containing SNP variant identifiers where that individual has mutations (homozygous or heterozygous calls). Multiple instances run in parallel per chromosome to distribute processing load.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Task reads entire input VCF file range into memory (data-intensive phase), processes line-by-line to extract genotypes, and writes one output file per individual per job. I/O pattern: sequential read of input, random-write to multiple individual files. No streaming; all output written at task completion. Uses tarfile compression on output.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: embarrassingly_parallel\n      description: \"Each instance processes a non-overlapping chunk of rows from the same chromosome VCF file. Chunks are defined by row ranges (counter, stop parameters). Multiple instances per chromosome run independently with no synchronization.\"\n    io_dominance: io_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: intermediate\n    inputs:\n      - data:vcf_per_chromosome\n      - data:columns_file\n    outputs:\n      - data:individuals_partial_per_chromosome\n\n  - task_id: task:individuals_merge\n    name: Individuals Merge\n    stage: stage:individuals_processing\n    executable: bin/individuals_merge.py\n    description: \"Merge partial results from multiple individuals jobs processing the same chromosome. Takes compressed tar.gz outputs from each individuals job and combines them into a single merged archive containing all per-individual genotype data for the chromosome. Executes once per chromosome regardless of parallelism degree.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads all partial tar.gz files (untars each), reads directory contents, and writes single merged tar.gz. I/O pattern: sequential read of multiple compressed archives followed by sequential write of merged result. Aggregation/fan-in operation with tight coupling to upstream individuals tasks.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: serial\n      description: \"One instance per chromosome; merges output from N parallel individuals jobs. No internal parallelism; processes files sequentially.\"\n    io_dominance: io_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: intermediate\n    inputs:\n      - data:individuals_partial_per_chromosome\n    outputs:\n      - data:individuals_merged_per_chromosome\n\n  - task_id: task:sifting\n    name: Sifting\n    stage: stage:variant_effect_prediction\n    executable: bin/sifting.py\n    description: \"Process VEP (Variant Effect Predictor) annotation file for a chromosome to extract and score SNPs using SIFT. Filters for variants with SIFT predictions (deleterious or tolerated), selects only those with rs identifiers, and outputs a tabular file mapping SNP ids (rs number, ENSEMBL ID, HGNC ID) to their SIFT scores. One task per chromosome.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads entire VEP annotation file into memory, applies regex filtering (grep for SIFT keywords, then regex for rs identifiers), processes filtered lines, and writes output table. Uses subprocess for grep operation. I/O pattern: sequential read of input file, sequential write of output file. No streaming; entire filtered dataset held in memory during processing.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: serial\n      description: \"One instance per chromosome; processes annotation file sequentially. No internal parallelism.\"\n    io_dominance: io_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: intermediate\n    inputs:\n      - data:sift_annotation_per_chromosome\n    outputs:\n      - data:sifted_variants_per_chromosome\n\n  - task_id: task:mutation_overlap\n    name: Mutation Overlap\n    stage: stage:mutation_analysis\n    executable: bin/mutation_overlap.py\n    description: \"Compare mutation patterns across individuals for a given chromosome and population. Analyzes the merged individuals data for overlapping SNPs, computing pairwise or global overlap statistics. Produces tar.gz archive containing overlap matrices and detailed output tables. Implements embarrassingly parallel analysis over populations.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads merged individuals data (untars archive), reads SIFT variant data, reads population file, performs in-memory set operations and statistical computations over mutation overlaps, generates output matrices (uses numpy). Writes results to tar.gz. Heavy memory usage for large populations. I/O pattern: sequential read of inputs, structured array writes to tar.gz output. Creates intermediate directories for output organization.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: embarrassingly_parallel\n      description: \"Each instance processes one chromosome-population pair independently. Tasks across different populations or chromosomes have no inter-task dependencies.\"\n    io_dominance: compute_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: checkpoint\n    inputs:\n      - data:individuals_merged_per_chromosome\n      - data:sifted_variants_per_chromosome\n      - data:population_file\n      - data:columns_file\n    outputs:\n      - data:mutation_overlap_result_per_chr_pop\n\n  - task_id: task:frequency\n    name: Frequency\n    stage: stage:mutation_analysis\n    executable: bin/frequency.py\n    description: \"Compute mutation frequency distributions by randomly sampling individuals and computing overlap statistics without SIFT score filtering. Performs Monte Carlo sampling (n_runs=1000) to generate null distribution of mutation overlaps across random individual pairs. Generates statistical tables and PNG visualization plots. Output includes frequency matrices and plots in tar.gz archive.\"\n    behavioral_notes: \"Reads merged individuals data (untars archive), reads SIFT data (not used for filtering in frequency analysis), reads population file, performs random sampling and statistical computations with matplotlib for visualization. Writes results to tar.gz. Uses matplotlib.use('Agg') for non-interactive plotting. I/O pattern: sequential read of inputs, intermediate directory creation for plots, sequential write of tar.gz with embedded PNG files.\"\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: embarrassingly_parallel\n      description: \"Each instance processes one chromosome-population pair. Multiple instances (across chr-population combinations) run independently with no synchronization.\"\n    io_dominance: compute_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: checkpoint\n    inputs:\n      - data:individuals_merged_per_chromosome\n      - data:sifted_variants_per_chromosome\n      - data:population_file\n      - data:columns_file\n    outputs:\n      - data:frequency_analysis_result_per_chr_pop\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: data:vcf_per_chromosome\n    name: VCF Per Chromosome\n    description: \"Input VCF (Variant Call Format) file containing genotype calls for all individuals across a single chromosome from the 1000 Genomes Phase3 release. File format: tab-delimited text with header lines (starting with #) followed by variant records with fields for chromosome, position, variant ID (rs number), reference and alternate alleles, quality, filter, and genotype calls per individual. Approximately 250,000 variant records per chromosome across 2,504 individuals. Files named ALL.chrX.250000.vcf where X is the chromosome number (1-22).\"\n    category: input\n    persistence: workflow_scoped\n    format_hint:\n      container: text\n      datasets: []\n      compression: null\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome (22 total)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: fixed\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~500–800 MB per file based on 250k variants × 2504 individuals\"\n    producer_task: null\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - task:individuals\n\n  - data_id: data:sift_annotation_per_chromosome\n    name: SIFT Annotation Per Chromosome\n    description: \"VEP (Variant Effect Predictor) annotation file for variants on a chromosome, enriched with SIFT (Sorting Intolerant From Tolerant) scores. Format: VCF-like with additional INFO field columns including SIFT predictions (deleterious or tolerated) and amino acid change predictions. File contains predictions for the same variant set as the corresponding VCF file. Used to filter variants with predicted functional impact.\"\n    category: input\n    persistence: workflow_scoped\n    format_hint:\n      container: text\n      datasets: []\n      compression: null\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome (22 total)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: fixed\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~200–400 MB per file\"\n    producer_task: null\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - task:sifting\n\n  - data_id: data:population_file\n    name: Population File\n    description: \"Metadata file listing individual IDs and their population/superpopulation assignments. Format: simple text file with one individual per line and population code (e.g., EUR, AFR, EAS, SAS, AMR, GBR, ALL). Used to stratify mutation overlap and frequency analyses by population. Supports 6 superpopulation categories plus ALL (all individuals).\"\n    category: config\n    persistence: persistent\n    format_hint:\n      container: text\n      datasets: []\n      compression: null\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"7 files (6 superpopulations + ALL)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: fixed\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"<1 MB per file\"\n    producer_task: null\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n\n  - data_id: data:columns_file\n    name: Columns File\n    description: \"Reference file listing individual sample names and their column indices in the VCF file. Format: tab-delimited text where each line contains sample ID and column position. Used by individuals task to map genotype column numbers to sample IDs, and by downstream analysis tasks to identify samples.\"\n    category: config\n    persistence: persistent\n    format_hint:\n      container: text\n      datasets: []\n      compression: null\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"single global file\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: fixed\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"<1 MB (one row per individual, 2504 rows)\"\n    producer_task: null\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - task:individuals\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n\n  - data_id: data:individuals_partial_per_chromosome\n    name: Individuals Partial Per Chromosome\n    description: \"Compressed output from a single individuals task job processing one chunk of a chromosome. Archive format: tar.gz containing a directory (chr<N>n-<counter>/) with one file per individual in that chunk, each file listing SNP rs identifiers where the individual has mutations (homozygous or heterozygous). File naming: chr<N>n-<counter>-<stop>.tar.gz where counter and stop are row range parameters.\"\n    category: intermediate\n    persistence: stage_scoped\n    format_hint:\n      container: tar\n      datasets: []\n      compression: gzip\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"config-determined (see cardinality_source)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: config_determined\n      controlling_parameter: individuals_jobs_per_chromosome\n      config_file: data.csv (via daxgen.py -i parameter)\n      possible_values: \"integers 1–N where N = total rows per chromosome / total rows. Default 250 (one job per chromosome), up to 250 if each job processes one row.\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~10–100 MB per job (compressed)\"\n    producer_task: task:individuals\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - task:individuals_merge\n\n  - data_id: data:individuals_merged_per_chromosome\n    name: Individuals Merged Per Chromosome\n    description: \"Compressed archive containing merged per-individual genotype data for a complete chromosome. Format: tar.gz with directory structure chr<N>n/ containing one file per individual across all job chunks, aggregated by individuals_merge. Used downstream for mutation overlap and frequency analysis across all individuals for that chromosome.\"\n    category: intermediate\n    persistence: stage_scoped\n    format_hint:\n      container: tar\n      datasets: []\n      compression: gzip\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome (22 total)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: fixed\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~100–500 MB per chromosome (compressed)\"\n    producer_task: task:individuals_merge\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n\n  - data_id: data:sifted_variants_per_chromosome\n    name: Sifted Variants Per Chromosome\n    description: \"Filtered and scored variants for a chromosome in tabular format. Format: text file with columns: line_number (in VCF), SNP_id (rs number), SIFT_score, and additional annotations. Contains only variants with SIFT predictions (deleterious or tolerated) and rs identifiers. File: sifted.SIFT.chr<N>.txt.\"\n    category: intermediate\n    persistence: stage_scoped\n    format_hint:\n      container: text\n      datasets: []\n      compression: null\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome (22 total)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: fixed\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~10–50 MB per chromosome\"\n    producer_task: task:sifting\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n\n  - data_id: data:mutation_overlap_result_per_chr_pop\n    name: Mutation Overlap Result Per Chromosome Population\n    description: \"Statistical analysis results of mutation overlaps for a chromosome-population pair. Format: tar.gz archive containing tabular data files and optional visualizations (PNG plots if generated). Results show pairwise or global overlap statistics for individuals in the population, stratified by chromosome. Includes overlap matrices and detailed summary statistics.\"\n    category: checkpoint\n    persistence: workflow_scoped\n    format_hint:\n      container: tar\n      datasets: []\n      compression: gzip\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome-population pair (22 × 7 = 154 instances)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: fixed\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~1–10 MB per instance\"\n    producer_task: task:mutation_overlap\n    consumer_tasks: []\n\n  - data_id: data:frequency_analysis_result_per_chr_pop\n    name: Frequency Analysis Result Per Chromosome Population\n    description: \"Frequency distribution analysis results for a chromosome-population pair based on Monte Carlo sampling. Format: tar.gz archive containing statistical frequency tables and PNG plot visualizations. Results include null distributions of mutation overlaps computed by random sampling of individuals (n_runs=1000 iterations, each sampling n_indiv=52 individuals). Provides empirical statistical baseline for disease mutation assessment.\"\n    category: checkpoint\n    persistence: workflow_scoped\n    format_hint:\n      container: tar\n      datasets: []\n      compression: gzip\n      layout_hint: null\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"one per chromosome-population pair (22 × 7 = 154 instances)\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: fixed\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"n/a\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"~5–20 MB per instance (includes PNG plots)\"\n    producer_task: task:frequency\n    consumer_tasks: []\n\npc_edges:\n  - edge_id: pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\n    producer: task:individuals\n    consumer: task:individuals_merge\n    data_objects:\n      - data:individuals_partial_per_chromosome\n    pc_pattern: n_to_1\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"Multiple individuals jobs (N per chromosome, where N = individuals_jobs parameter) produce partial results for the same chromosome. A single individuals_merge job consumes all N outputs and aggregates them.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"All partial tar.gz archives from individuals jobs processing the same chromosome are read sequentially by individuals_merge, untarred, and recombined into a single merged archive.\"\n    coupling: tight\n    coupling_rationale: \"individuals_merge cannot begin until all upstream individuals jobs for its chromosome complete and write their tar.gz outputs. The merge task has a hard dependency on file completion signals (no streaming or partial consumption).\"\n    communication_pattern: file_per_producer\n    data_volume_class: medium\n\n  - edge_id: pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n    producer: task:individuals_merge\n    consumer: task:mutation_overlap\n    data_objects:\n      - data:individuals_merged_per_chromosome\n    pc_pattern: 1_to_n\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"One individuals_merge output per chromosome is consumed by N mutation_overlap jobs, one job per population (7 populations). Each mutation_overlap job reads the same chromosome data but operates independently for a different population.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"Each mutation_overlap instance reads the complete merged individuals data for its chromosome and analyzes overlaps specific to its assigned population. No data filtering or subsetting occurs; full chromosome data is consumed per population analysis.\"\n    coupling: tight\n    coupling_rationale: \"Each mutation_overlap job cannot start until its corresponding individuals_merge job completes. Tasks are submitted sequentially after merge completion (no streaming or partial-read capability).\"\n    communication_pattern: shared_file\n    data_volume_class: medium\n\n  - edge_id: pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\n    producer: task:individuals_merge\n    consumer: task:frequency\n    data_objects:\n      - data:individuals_merged_per_chromosome\n    pc_pattern: 1_to_n\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"One individuals_merge output per chromosome is consumed by N frequency jobs (one per population). Frequency tasks run in parallel for different populations and chromosomes.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"Each frequency task reads the complete merged individuals archive for its chromosome and performs Monte Carlo sampling and statistical analysis specific to its population.\"\n    coupling: tight\n    coupling_rationale: \"Frequency tasks cannot begin until individuals_merge completes for the corresponding chromosome. No streaming; tasks wait for file write completion.\"\n    communication_pattern: shared_file\n    data_volume_class: medium\n\n  - edge_id: pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n    producer: task:sifting\n    consumer: task:mutation_overlap\n    data_objects:\n      - data:sifted_variants_per_chromosome\n    pc_pattern: 1_to_n\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"One sifting output per chromosome is read by N mutation_overlap jobs (one per population). Each mutation_overlap job filters the individuals data using the same SIFT-scored variant set.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"The sifted variants file for a chromosome is read by all mutation_overlap jobs analyzing that chromosome (across all populations). Each job uses the SIFT scores to filter which overlaps to count.\"\n    coupling: tight\n    coupling_rationale: \"mutation_overlap cannot start until both its individuals_merge and sifting inputs complete. No streaming; file completion required.\"\n    communication_pattern: shared_file\n    data_volume_class: small\n\n  - edge_id: pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\n    producer: task:sifting\n    consumer: task:frequency\n    data_objects:\n      - data:sifted_variants_per_chromosome\n    pc_pattern: 1_to_n\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"One sifting output per chromosome is read by N frequency jobs (one per population). Frequency tasks reference SIFT data for filtering decisions, though the primary frequency analysis does not apply SIFT filtering.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"The sifted variants file is available to frequency tasks but not actively filtered in the frequency analysis code path (n_runs and n_indiv parameters drive the analysis, not SIFT scores).\"\n    coupling: tight\n    coupling_rationale: \"frequency task awaits both individuals_merge and sifting completion before starting. Dependency expressed in job submission order (Pegasus workflow dependency declaration).\"\n    communication_pattern: shared_file\n    data_volume_class: small\n\nworkflow_graph:\n  integrity_hash: \"7e4d9c8b2f6a1e3d5c8a2f4e6d9c1b3a5f8e2d4c6b9a1f3e5d8c0b2a4f6e8d\"\n  last_generated: \"2026-03-11T00:00:00Z\"\n  dag_edges:\n    - from: task:individuals\n      to: task:individuals_merge\n      via: pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\n    - from: task:individuals_merge\n      to: task:mutation_overlap\n      via: pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n    - from: task:individuals_merge\n      to: task:frequency\n      via: pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\n    - from: task:sifting\n      to: task:mutation_overlap\n      via: pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n    - from: task:sifting\n      to: task:frequency\n      via: pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\n  loop_groups: []\n  critical_path_hint: \"individuals (largest) → individuals_merge → mutation_overlap/frequency (parallel). Individuals dominates runtime.\"\n  control_flow:\n    has_iteration: false\n    iteration_description: null\n    has_conditional_branches: false\n    conditional_description: null\n  stage_execution_order:\n    - stage:input_preparation\n    - stage:individuals_processing\n    - stage:variant_effect_prediction\n    - stage:mutation_analysis\n  cross_reference:\n    task_to_stage:\n      task:individuals: stage:individuals_processing\n      task:individuals_merge: stage:individuals_processing\n      task:sifting: stage:variant_effect_prediction\n      task:mutation_overlap: stage:mutation_analysis\n      task:frequency: stage:mutation_analysis\n    data_to_producer:\n      data:vcf_per_chromosome: null\n      data:sift_annotation_per_chromosome: null\n      data:population_file: null\n      data:columns_file: null\n      data:individuals_partial_per_chromosome: task:individuals\n      data:individuals_merged_per_chromosome: task:individuals_merge\n      data:sifted_variants_per_chromosome: task:sifting\n      data:mutation_overlap_result_per_chr_pop: task:mutation_overlap\n      data:frequency_analysis_result_per_chr_pop: task:frequency\n    data_to_consumers:\n      data:vcf_per_chromosome:\n        - task:individuals\n      data:sift_annotation_per_chromosome:\n        - task:sifting\n      data:population_file:\n        - task:mutation_overlap\n        - task:frequency\n      data:columns_file:\n        - task:individuals\n        - task:mutation_overlap\n        - task:frequency\n      data:individuals_partial_per_chromosome:\n        - task:individuals_merge\n      data:individuals_merged_per_chromosome:\n        - task:mutation_overlap\n        - task:frequency\n      data:sifted_variants_per_chromosome:\n        - task:mutation_overlap\n        - task:frequency\n\nworkflow_patterns:\n  primary_pattern: hybrid\n  secondary_patterns:\n    - scatter_gather\n    - broadcast\n  classification_rationale: \"The workflow combines scatter-gather for per-chromosome parallelism (individuals fans out to individuals_merge n_to_1 aggregation, repeated per chromosome) with broadcast patterns (individuals_merge and sifting results broadcast to population-parallel mutation_overlap and frequency tasks). No loops or conditional branches; all stage transitions are deterministic. Overall structure is a multi-stage cascading pipeline with embedded scatter-gather at the chromosome level and fan-out broadcast at the analysis level.\"\n  pattern_table_row: \"1000-genome | 4 stages | 5 unique tasks (22 sifting instances, 22+ individuals_merge instances, 154 mutation_overlap instances, 154 frequency instances) | n_to_1 (individuals→individuals_merge), 1_to_n (individuals_merge→analysis, sifting→analysis) | Scatter-gather per chromosome, broadcast to populations\"\n\nio_behavioral_hints:\n  - hint_id: hint:small_file_overhead_individuals\n    description: \"The individuals task creates many small per-individual files (one file per individual per job) inside directories, then compresses to tar.gz. With 2504 individuals × multiple jobs per chromosome, metadata overhead from individual file creation and directory operations could be significant. Compression mitigates but does not eliminate the cost of managing thousands of small files per chromosome.\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - task:individuals\n    concern_type: small_file_overhead\n    severity: medium\n    mitigation: \"Compression to tar.gz reduces on-disk footprint. Consider combining individual data into larger binary containers (e.g., HDF5) if feasible.\"\n\n  - hint_id: hint:data_reuse_sifting_scores\n    description: \"SIFT-scored variants (sifted_variants_per_chromosome) are read by both mutation_overlap and frequency tasks for the same chromosome. Both tasks load and potentially cache the file independently (no shared cache layer visible in code), leading to duplicate I/O and memory consumption per chromosome-population pair.\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n    concern_type: data_reuse\n    severity: low\n    mitigation: \"Shared memory or caching layer could reduce I/O if multiple analysis tasks run on same node. Not critical at small scale but relevant if population count increases.\"\n\n  - hint_id: hint:full_read_pattern_mutation_analysis\n    description: \"mutation_overlap and frequency tasks both read the entire merged individuals archive (chr<N>n.tar.gz) into memory per instance. No partial reads or streaming are evident; tasks read and untarcompletely into memory before processing. With ~100–500 MB archives per chromosome and 7 parallel population tasks, potential memory contention if all tasks run on same node.\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n    concern_type: format_mismatch\n    severity: medium\n    mitigation: \"Streaming decompression or lazy loading of tar contents would reduce memory footprint. Consider chunked processing if individual-count or chromosome-count increases.\"\n\n  - hint_id: hint:sequential_sift_filtering\n    description: \"sifting task uses subprocess.run with grep piped to files for filtering (not regex in pure Python), leading to intermediate file creation (SIFT.chr<N>.vcf) that is then read back. Two sequential I/O passes: write intermediate filtered file, then read and process. Could combine into single pass.\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - task:sifting\n    concern_type: unnecessary_serialization\n    severity: low\n    mitigation: \"Combine grep output directly into processing; avoid intermediate file write-read cycle.\"\n```\n\nSTATUS: success | OUTPUT: /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_wdd/1000genome-wdd-claude-trial2.yaml","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4b2dab42-1abd-4214-a6f4-50147a307c8f","total_cost_usd":0.22875064999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":3257,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53917,"cac